            <ArticleTitle>[Rare diagnosis as the etiology of abdominal pain after cholecystectomy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>101-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1024/1661-8157/a001900</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a 77-year old female patient with abdominal pain in the upper right part. In the computertomography we had the suspicion of a rare small bowel diverticulitis which was confirmed in laparoscopic and histopathologic diagnostics. After surgical excision the patient was free of symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
